  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "What This Handbook Covers",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "What This Handbook Covers",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Buckets and Objects",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bucket==: globally unique name, one Region",
                "Object = key + data (up to ==50 TB==) + metadata",
                "Single PUT max ==5 GB==; use multipart above",
                "'Folders' are just key prefixes with `/`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Storage Classes and Lifecycle",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "Use",
                "Minimum"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Standard",
                  "frequent",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Intelligent-Tiering",
                  "unknown",
                  "none"
                ],
                [
                  "Standard-IA / One Zone-IA",
                  "infrequent",
                  "30 d"
                ],
                [
                  "Glacier Instant / Flexible",
                  "archive",
                  "90 d"
                ],
                [
                  "Deep Archive",
                  "archive",
                  "180 d"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Lifecycle = filter + ==Transition== (down only) + ==Expiration==",
                "Also abort incomplete multipart uploads",
                "Archived objects need a ==restore== before GET"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Versioning",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "States: unversioned, enabled, suspended; never removable",
                "Plain DELETE adds a ==delete marker==",
                "DELETE with `versionId` is permanent",
                "Expire noncurrent versions to cut cost"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Policies, Block Public Access, Presigned URLs",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Explicit Deny== beats any Allow",
                "`bucket` for ListBucket, `bucket/*` for GetObject",
                "==Block Public Access== overrides public policies and ACLs",
                "Presigned URL: time-limited access to one object"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws s3 presign s3://bucket/key --expires-in 3600"
              ],
              "note": "CLI makes GET URLs only; PUT URLs need an SDK"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Buckets, Objects and Strong Consistency",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Buckets, Objects and Strong Consistency",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bucket and Object",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bucket: ==globally unique name==, lives in **one Region**",
                "Object = key + data (up to ==50 TB==) + metadata",
                "==Flat namespace==: 'folders' are only key prefixes with `/`",
                "Single PUT capped at ==5 GB=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Uploads and Consistency",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Over 5 GB: ==multipart upload==; prefer it above 100 MB",
                "Incomplete uploads are **billed**: abort or lifecycle-clean",
                "{green:Strong} read-after-write: PUT, overwrite, DELETE, LIST",
                "No eventual-consistency window",
                "Same key, concurrent writers: ==last writer wins=="
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Everyday Commands",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws s3 cp file s3://bucket/key",
                "aws s3 ls s3://bucket/prefix/",
                "aws s3 sync ./dir s3://bucket/dir --delete",
                "aws s3 rm s3://bucket/key --recursive"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Careful",
              "text": "`sync --delete` removes destination objects missing from the source."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**File system?** No, a flat key-value object store",
                "**Eventually consistent?** No, strongly consistent today",
                "**Same key at once?** Last writer wins",
                "**Multipart when?** Over 5 GB, ideally over 100 MB"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Storage Classes and Lifecycle Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Storage Classes and Lifecycle Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Classes and minimums",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "Use",
                "Min",
                "Get"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Standard",
                  "frequent",
                  "-",
                  "ms"
                ],
                [
                  "Intelligent-Tiering",
                  "unknown, auto-tiers",
                  "-",
                  "ms"
                ],
                [
                  "Standard-IA",
                  "infrequent",
                  "30d, 128 KB",
                  "ms"
                ],
                [
                  "One Zone-IA",
                  "infrequent, 1 AZ",
                  "30d, 128 KB",
                  "ms"
                ],
                [
                  "Glacier Instant",
                  "archive",
                  "90d",
                  "ms"
                ],
                [
                  "Glacier Flexible",
                  "archive",
                  "90d",
                  "min-hrs"
                ],
                [
                  "Deep Archive",
                  "archive",
                  "180d",
                  "~12h / ~48h"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 1
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{red:Early delete} is still charged",
                "Archived objects need a ==restore== before GET",
                "Flexible: Expedited, Standard, Bulk"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Lifecycle rules",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Filter",
                    "sub": "prefix, tag, size",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Transition",
                    "sub": "days, down only",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Expiration",
                    "sub": "delete",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Waterfall: Standard → IA → Glacier → Deep Archive",
                "Also set `AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload`, `NoncurrentVersionExpiration`",
                "Rules run async, ==about daily=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Tiering over IA?** Unknown access; no retrieval fee",
                "**Back to Standard?** Transitions only go down; copy instead",
                "**Tiny objects to Glacier?** Per-object costs beat savings",
                "**Old versions?** Expire noncurrent versions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Versioning and Delete Behaviour",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Versioning and Delete Behaviour",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Three States",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Unversioned==, ==enabled==, ==suspended==",
                "Enabled can only be **suspended**, never removed",
                "Existing versions are **kept**"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Overwrite and Delete",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Action",
                "Result"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "PUT same key",
                  "New **version ID**, now current"
                ],
                [
                  "DELETE, no versionId",
                  "Adds a **delete marker**; object looks gone"
                ],
                [
                  "DELETE with versionId",
                  "==Permanent== removal of that version"
                ],
                [
                  "Delete the marker",
                  "Object is **restored**"
                ],
                [
                  "MFA Delete",
                  "Needs MFA for permanent deletes, versioning changes"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Still billed",
              "text": "Older versions stay after a delete marker and keep costing storage."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Enable and Inspect",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket b --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled",
                "aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket b --prefix key"
              ],
              "note": "lists versions and delete markers"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Recover a deleted object?** Delete the marker, or copy an older versionId",
                "**Why does cost grow?** Every version is billed; expire ==noncurrent== versions with lifecycle",
                "**Disable versioning?** No, only suspend; old versions stay",
                "**Current vs noncurrent?** Latest version vs all older ones"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Bucket Policies, Block Public Access and Presigned URLs",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Bucket Policies, Block Public Access and Presigned URLs",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Bucket Policy",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Resource-based **JSON** policy, ==20 KB== max",
                "Needs a `Principal`; can grant ==cross-account== access",
                "Explicit {red:Deny} beats any Allow",
                "Same account: an Allow in IAM **or** policy"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "ARN",
                "Covers",
                "Example"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`arn:aws:s3:::bucket`",
                  "bucket",
                  "`ListBucket`"
                ],
                [
                  "`arn:aws:s3:::bucket/*`",
                  "objects",
                  "`GetObject`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "One ARN form only gives ==AccessDenied== for the other"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Block Public Access",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Four switches: block public ACLs, ignore public ACLs, block public policies, restrict public buckets",
                "Account and bucket level; ==overrides== policies and ACLs",
                "{green:On by default} for new buckets",
                "ACLs off by default (`BucketOwnerEnforced`)"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Presigned URL",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Time-limited ==GET== for one object (CLI: GET only; PUT needs SDK)",
                "`aws s3 presign s3://bucket/key --expires-in 3600`",
                "Default **3600 s**",
                "Max **7 days** with IAM user keys",
                "Role or session credentials expire it earlier"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Share a private object?** Send a presigned URL.",
                "**Early expiry?** Role or session credentials end first.",
                "**Policy vs IAM?** They combine; an explicit Deny wins.",
                "**Org-wide?** Enforce Block Public Access on every account.",
                "**Leaked URL?** Use short expiry and a least-privilege signer."
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "S3 Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "S3 Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Model",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Bucket==: globally unique name, one Region",
                "==Object==: key + data up to ==50 TB==; ==5 GB== per PUT",
                "Flat keys; ==strong== read-after-write; ==last writer wins=="
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Classes and Versioning",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Class",
                "Minimum"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "IA classes",
                  "30 days, 128 KB"
                ],
                [
                  "Glacier Instant / Flexible",
                  "90 days"
                ],
                [
                  "Deep Archive",
                  "180 days"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Intelligent-Tiering==: unknown patterns",
                "Archived objects need a ==restore==",
                "Versioning: ==suspend== only, never removed",
                "Delete adds a ==marker==; ==versionId== delete is permanent",
                "Lifecycle: expire noncurrent, abort incomplete multipart"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Access",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Explicit ==Deny== wins",
                "`bucket` ARN: bucket actions; `bucket/*`: objects",
                "==Block Public Access== overrides public policies and ACLs",
                "Keep ACLs disabled"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Commands",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "aws s3 cp f s3://b/k",
                "aws s3 ls s3://b/p/",
                "aws s3 sync ./d s3://b/d --delete",
                "aws s3 rm s3://b/k --recursive",
                "aws s3 presign s3://b/k --expires-in 3600",
                "aws s3api put-bucket-versioning --bucket b --versioning-configuration Status=Enabled",
                "aws s3api put-bucket-lifecycle-configuration --bucket b --lifecycle-configuration file://l.json",
                "aws s3api list-object-versions --bucket b"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A policy allows `s3:GetObject` on `arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket`. Reads still get AccessDenied. Why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "GetObject is an object action, so the Resource must be `arn:aws:s3:::my-bucket/*`.",
                "The bare bucket ARN only covers bucket actions like ListBucket."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Versioning is on. You run `aws s3 rm s3://b/report.csv` and `ls` shows nothing. Is the data gone?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "No. A plain delete only adds a **delete marker**.",
                "Older versions remain and are still billed.",
                "Delete the marker by its versionId to restore the object."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A 20 KB object moves to Standard-IA and is deleted 10 days later. Did that save money?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Probably not. IA bills at least 128 KB.",
                "It also bills a 30-day minimum, so the early delete is still charged."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
